d 'TSVY': module to produce point-estimate table and Wald/Bonferroni/CLD test, by level of aggregation and year, using svylet as the estimation engine
d
d    tsvy builds, in one pass, the table that a researcher working
d with repeated cross-sections or panel waves of a complex survey  
d  usually needs: point estimates broken down by level of
d aggregation (national, regional, local, ...) and by year,
d together with    a test of whether each level's estimate actually
d changed from year to year. It loops over every level of
d aggregation named in	  caida(), running the same
d omnibus-F/Bonferroni/CLD computation as svylet once per (level x
d value x [sexovar value])    combination, and accumulates one row
d per year in a frame that is ready to reshape wide and export --
d so the point-estimate    table and the F/Bonferroni/CLD test come
d from the very same call, with no separate pass to keep aligned by
d hand. 
d
d KW: complex survey data
d KW: taabulations
d KW: export
d
d Requires: Stata version 14 and svylet from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260827
d
d Author: Andres Talavera Cuya,   Direccion Nacional de Censos y Encuestas -- INEI Peru
d Support: email talaveracuya@@gmail.com
d
f tsvy.ado
f tsvy.sthlp
f tsvy_es.sthlp
